libsmb2, the SMB2/3 client library by Ronnie Sahlberg and contributors
https://github.com/sahlberg/libsmb2, commit fc710a3ebd58a3c15d0ef24322f748e38a3d3a90

Licence: LGPL-2.1-or-later for lib/ and include/ (COPYING, LICENCE-LGPL-2.1.txt).
Only the client library is here: lib/ (the sources listed in sources.txt, and
their headers) and include/. The DCE/RPC library, the examples, utilities and
tests are left out.

Porpoise reads games on a network share with it (src/porpoise_netfs.cpp).
tools/build.sh compiles each file in sources.txt as C with ps5/config.h.

Changes from upstream:
- ps5/config.h: the configuration for the PS5's FreeBSD headers (upstream
  makes config.h with CMake or autoconf; _U_ comes from lib/CMakeLists.txt).
- lib/socket.c: SO_NOSIGPIPE on the client socket, so a write to a connection
  the server has closed fails with EPIPE instead of ending the app.
- The build renames getaddrinfo, freeaddrinfo, getlogin_r, gethostname and
  __isthreaded to src/porpoise_netfs.cpp's (the console's libc has no resolver
  in the modules Porpoise loads), and sets SOL_TCP to IPPROTO_TCP.
